{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781049090162,"sessionID":"ses_15133c710fferRwlSke4x56SqF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"tooluse_mcDQ37pHwXXdPI8vl9SzB9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\GHC\\repos\\OMEGA_QUANT\\.ly_state\\session\\p10_l2_gate_tuning_partial_metadata_fix_prompt_20260610.md"},"output":"<path>C:\\Users\\GHC\\repos\\OMEGA_QUANT\\.ly_state\\session\\p10_l2_gate_tuning_partial_metadata_fix_prompt_20260610.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # [L2-Impl:Role9-BackendEngineer] P10 Gate Tuning Partial-Horizon Metadata Fix\n2: \n3: You are L2 implementation only. Do not audit/approve.\n4: \n5: ## Scope\n6: Allowed files only:\n7: - `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`\n8: - `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`\n9: - `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_partial_metadata_fix_report_20260610.md`\n10: \n11: ## Read first\n12: - `.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md`\n13: \n14: ## Required fix\n15: \n16: Role20 found JSON/fold reporting can persist wrong horizon metadata in partial-success folds:\n17: - `horizon_details` includes excluded + included horizons.\n18: - Current code uses first requested horizon metadata, not first included/successful horizon.\n19: - If horizon 1 excluded but horizon 3 included, FoldMetrics/JSON can report excluded metadata while signal uses horizon 3.\n20: \n21: Fix:\n22: 1. In `run_fold()` multi-horizon path, choose metadata/gated_alphas/gate_results from the first included horizon, not first requested key.\n23: 2. Better if surgical: persist per-horizon diagnostics for all requested horizons in `FoldMetrics.gate_metadata`, e.g. include `horizon_details_summary` or `all_horizon_gate_metadata` with included/excluded status. But minimum: first included horizon metadata must be truthful.\n24: 3. Ensure fallback path remains unchanged.\n25: \n26: Tests:\n27: - Add a test where `horizon_details` or run_fold scenario has horizon 1 excluded and horizon 3 included, then assert FoldMetrics.gate_metadata corresponds to included horizon 3 metadata.\n28: - If easier, unit-test helper/function that selects reported horizon metadata.\n29: - Ensure existing P10 tests still pass.\n30: \n31: Verification:\n32: ```powershell\n33: python -m pytest tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py -q\n34: python -m pytest tests/phase35/ -q\n35: ```\n36: \n37: Report:\n38: Write `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_partial_metadata_fix_report_20260610.md` with fix/test results.\n39: \n40: Do not commit/push.\n\n(End of file - total 40 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# [L2-Impl:Role9-BackendEngineer] P10 Gate Tuning Partial-Horizon Metadata Fix\n\nYou are L2 implementation only. Do not audit/approve.\n\n## Scope\nAllowed files only:\n- `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`\n- `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`\n- `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_partial_metadata_fix_report_20260610.md`\n\n## Read first\n- `.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md`\n\n## Required fix\n\nRole20 found JSON/fold reporting can persist wrong horizon metadata in partial-success folds:\n- `horizon_details` includes excluded + included horizons.\n- Current code uses first requested horizon metadata, not first included/successful horizon.\n- If horizon 1 excluded but horizon 3 included, FoldMetrics/JSON can report excluded metadata while signal uses horizon 3.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\Users\\GHC\\repos\\OMEGA_QUANT\\.ly_state\\session\\p10_l2_gate_tuning_partial_metadata_fix_prompt_20260610.md","text":"# [L2-Impl:Role9-BackendEngineer] P10 Gate Tuning Partial-Horizon Metadata Fix\n\nYou are L2 implementation only. Do not audit/approve.\n\n## Scope\nAllowed files only:\n- `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`\n- `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`\n- `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_partial_metadata_fix_report_20260610.md`\n\n## Read first\n- `.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md`\n\n## Required fix\n\nRole20 found JSON/fold reporting can persist wrong horizon metadata in partial-success folds:\n- `horizon_details` includes excluded + included horizons.\n- Current code uses first requested horizon metadata, not first included/successful horizon.\n- If horizon 1 excluded but horizon 3 included, FoldMetrics/JSON can report excluded metadata while signal uses horizon 3.\n\nFix:\n1. In `run_fold()` multi-horizon path, choose metadata/gated_alphas/gate_results from the first included horizon, not first requested key.\n2. Better if surgical: persist per-horizon diagnostics for all requested horizons in `FoldMetrics.gate_metadata`, e.g. include `horizon_details_summary` or `all_horizon_gate_metadata` with included/excluded status. But minimum: first included horizon metadata must be truthful.\n3. Ensure fallback path remains unchanged.\n\nTests:\n- Add a test where `horizon_details` or run_fold scenario has horizon 1 excluded and horizon 3 included, then assert FoldMetrics.gate_metadata corresponds to included horizon 3 metadata.\n- If easier, unit-test helper/function that selects reported horizon metadata.\n- Ensure existing P10 tests still pass.\n\nVerification:\n```powershell\npython -m pytest tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py -q\npython -m pytest tests/phase35/ -q\n```\n\nReport:\nWrite `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_partial_metadata_fix_report_20260610.md` with fix/test results.\n\nDo not commit/push.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":40,"totalLines":40,"truncated":false}},"title":".ly_state\\session\\p10_l2_gate_tuning_partial_metadata_fix_prompt_20260610.md","time":{"start":1781049090143,"end":1781049090159}},"id":"prt_eaecc6050001VjIGK723bg6N5v","sessionID":"ses_15133c710fferRwlSke4x56SqF","messageID":"msg_eaecc3a78001eu34VavOYjzMt5"}}
