{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781049098953,"sessionID":"ses_15133c710fferRwlSke4x56SqF","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"tooluse_y8THNKzOxZVPek5HfZgVhe","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\GHC\\repos\\OMEGA_QUANT\\.ly_state\\session\\audit_reports\\role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md"},"output":"<path>C:\\Users\\GHC\\repos\\OMEGA_QUANT\\.ly_state\\session\\audit_reports\\role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Role20 P10 Gate Tuning Compliance Audit - 2026-06-10\n2: \n3: ## Gate Contract\n4: \n5: - l3_session_id: role20-p10-gate-compliance-20260610T064600+0700\n6: - l3_session_key: codex:role20:p10-gate-compliance:20260610T064600+0700\n7: - audit_report_path: .ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md\n8: - final_verdict: [NEEDS_FIX]\n9: \n10: ## Audit Header\n11: \n12: - Role: [L3-Audit:Role20-ComplianceOfficer]\n13: - Verdict: [NEEDS_FIX]\n14: - PIT Safety: PASS\n15: - Role Compliance: PASS\n16: - Scope: Compliance audit of P10 gate tuning after Role21 approval for `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`, `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py`, `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`, and supplied L2/L3 reports.\n17: \n18: ## Findings\n19: \n20: ### P1 - JSON/fold reporting can persist the wrong horizon metadata after partial horizon success\n21: \n22: Evidence:\n23: \n24: - `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1652-1695` stores `horizon_details` for both included and excluded horizons, in requested-horizon insertion order.\n25: - `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1702-1724` only falls back to T+5 baseline when no horizons survive or when blend quality is non-positive. A partial-success case can continue on the normal multi-horizon path.\n26: - `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1755-1762` says it uses the first successful horizon, but actually uses `first_horizon = list(horizon_details.keys())[0]`. That is the first requested horizon, which can be excluded.\n27: - `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:2118-2137` writes that selected `gate_metadata`, `gate_results`, and `gated_alphas` into `FoldMetrics`.\n28: - `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:60-73` and `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:376` persist the `FoldMetrics.gate_metadata` and aliases into JSON.\n29: \n30: Impact:\n31: \n32: If horizon 1 is excluded but horizon 3 or 5 is included and the blend succeeds, JSON can report `selection_source: excluded`, `used_fallback_candidates: false`, empty `gated_alphas`, and gate counts from the excluded horizon while the actual signal came from a later included horizon. If the included later horizon used relaxed fallback candidates, that fallback label is not reliably persisted. This violates focus item 2 and item 6: fallback candidates must be labeled and persisted, and JSON/reporting must be truthful.\n33: \n34: Required fix:\n35: \n36: Persist metadata from the included horizon(s), not the first requested horizon. Minimum acceptable fix: select the first horizon where `included == True`. Better fix: persist per-horizon diagnostics for all requested horizons, including included/excluded status, gate metadata, quality metrics, and blend weight.\n37: \n38: Test gap:\n39: \n40: - `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:303-321` covers partial horizon success only at `_blend_horizon_signals()` level.\n41: - Existing serialization tests at `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:1243-1311` verify a supplied metadata object is serialized, but do not verify `run_fold()` chooses truthful metadata in partial-success scenarios.\n42: \n43: ## Compliance Checklist\n44: \n45: 1. Relaxed gate explicit opt-in only; strict defaults unchanged: PASS\n46:    - Engine defaults are strict at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:188-194`.\n47:    - CLI defaults are strict at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:167-182`.\n48:    - Strict zero-pass exclusion remains at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1303-1307`.\n49: \n50: 2. FAIL strings are not counted as pass; fallback candidates labeled and persisted: FAIL\n51:    - FAIL string counting is fixed by `_is_gate_verdict_pass()` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:37-93` and robust gate counts at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1294-1297`.\n52:    - Fallback labeling exists at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1431-1442` and JSON serialization exists at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:60-73`.\n53:    - Persistence is not truthful in partial-success folds because `run_fold()` can copy metadata from an excluded first requested horizon.\n54: \n55: 3. Relaxed fallback candidates do not bypass final-objective signed quality filter: PASS\n56:    - Final-objective train/validation IC is mapped into `train_ic`/`validation_ic` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1394-1422`.\n57:    - Signed quality filter rejects single non-positive horizon and all non-positive blends at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1509-1541`; no `abs()` fallback observed.\n58: \n59: 4. All invalid/non-positive horizons fallback T+5 baseline: PASS with reporting caveat\n60:    - Missing return columns produce excluded horizon metadata at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1222-1235`.\n61:    - All horizon failure triggers baseline `return_col` fallback at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1702-1735`; script sets `RETURN_HORIZON = 5` and `return_col = f'fwd_ret_{RETURN_HORIZON}'` at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:218-319`.\n62:    - Non-positive quality triggers baseline fallback at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1510-1541` and `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1715-1724`.\n63: \n64: 5. PIT safety/no lookahead: gate and weights use train/validation only: PASS\n65:    - Per-horizon embargo before train/validation split at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1237-1268`.\n66:    - Gate validation uses `val_actual`, not test data, at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1286-1292`.\n67:    - Blend quality metrics are computed on `train_actual`/`val_actual` against final objective at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1394-1422`.\n68: \n69: 6. JSON/reporting truthful for compliance: FAIL\n70:    - Same P1 finding: persisted fold metadata can describe an excluded horizon rather than the included/blended horizon.\n71: \n72: ## Verification Run\n73: \n74: - `python -m pytest tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py -q`: 42 passed.\n75: - `python -m pytest tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py::TestP10GateTuningCLIPersist -q`: 3 passed.\n76: - Warnings observed: Vnstock update notice, pandas/numpy warnings, and pytest cache path warning. No test failures.\n77: - Code-review graph minimal-context call timed out after 120 seconds; direct source/test/report audit completed.\n78: \n79: ## Final Verdict\n80: \n81: [NEEDS_FIX]\n\n(End of file - total 81 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Role20 P10 Gate Tuning Compliance Audit - 2026-06-10\n\n## Gate Contract\n\n- l3_session_id: role20-p10-gate-compliance-20260610T064600+0700\n- l3_session_key: codex:role20:p10-gate-compliance:20260610T064600+0700\n- audit_report_path: .ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md\n- final_verdict: [NEEDS_FIX]\n\n## Audit Header\n\n- Role: [L3-Audit:Role20-ComplianceOfficer]\n- Verdict: [NEEDS_FIX]\n- PIT Safety: PASS\n- Role Compliance: PASS\n- Scope: Compliance audit of P10 gate tuning after Role21 approval for `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`, `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py`, `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`, and supplied L2/L3 reports.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 - JSON/fold reporting can persist the wrong horizon metadata after partial horizon success","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\Users\\GHC\\repos\\OMEGA_QUANT\\.ly_state\\session\\audit_reports\\role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md","text":"# Role20 P10 Gate Tuning Compliance Audit - 2026-06-10\n\n## Gate Contract\n\n- l3_session_id: role20-p10-gate-compliance-20260610T064600+0700\n- l3_session_key: codex:role20:p10-gate-compliance:20260610T064600+0700\n- audit_report_path: .ly_state/session/audit_reports/role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md\n- final_verdict: [NEEDS_FIX]\n\n## Audit Header\n\n- Role: [L3-Audit:Role20-ComplianceOfficer]\n- Verdict: [NEEDS_FIX]\n- PIT Safety: PASS\n- Role Compliance: PASS\n- Scope: Compliance audit of P10 gate tuning after Role21 approval for `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`, `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py`, `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`, and supplied L2/L3 reports.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 - JSON/fold reporting can persist the wrong horizon metadata after partial horizon success\n\nEvidence:\n\n- `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1652-1695` stores `horizon_details` for both included and excluded horizons, in requested-horizon insertion order.\n- `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1702-1724` only falls back to T+5 baseline when no horizons survive or when blend quality is non-positive. A partial-success case can continue on the normal multi-horizon path.\n- `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1755-1762` says it uses the first successful horizon, but actually uses `first_horizon = list(horizon_details.keys())[0]`. That is the first requested horizon, which can be excluded.\n- `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:2118-2137` writes that selected `gate_metadata`, `gate_results`, and `gated_alphas` into `FoldMetrics`.\n- `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:60-73` and `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:376` persist the `FoldMetrics.gate_metadata` and aliases into JSON.\n\nImpact:\n\nIf horizon 1 is excluded but horizon 3 or 5 is included and the blend succeeds, JSON can report `selection_source: excluded`, `used_fallback_candidates: false`, empty `gated_alphas`, and gate counts from the excluded horizon while the actual signal came from a later included horizon. If the included later horizon used relaxed fallback candidates, that fallback label is not reliably persisted. This violates focus item 2 and item 6: fallback candidates must be labeled and persisted, and JSON/reporting must be truthful.\n\nRequired fix:\n\nPersist metadata from the included horizon(s), not the first requested horizon. Minimum acceptable fix: select the first horizon where `included == True`. Better fix: persist per-horizon diagnostics for all requested horizons, including included/excluded status, gate metadata, quality metrics, and blend weight.\n\nTest gap:\n\n- `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:303-321` covers partial horizon success only at `_blend_horizon_signals()` level.\n- Existing serialization tests at `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:1243-1311` verify a supplied metadata object is serialized, but do not verify `run_fold()` chooses truthful metadata in partial-success scenarios.\n\n## Compliance Checklist\n\n1. Relaxed gate explicit opt-in only; strict defaults unchanged: PASS\n   - Engine defaults are strict at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:188-194`.\n   - CLI defaults are strict at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:167-182`.\n   - Strict zero-pass exclusion remains at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1303-1307`.\n\n2. FAIL strings are not counted as pass; fallback candidates labeled and persisted: FAIL\n   - FAIL string counting is fixed by `_is_gate_verdict_pass()` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:37-93` and robust gate counts at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1294-1297`.\n   - Fallback labeling exists at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1431-1442` and JSON serialization exists at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:60-73`.\n   - Persistence is not truthful in partial-success folds because `run_fold()` can copy metadata from an excluded first requested horizon.\n\n3. Relaxed fallback candidates do not bypass final-objective signed quality filter: PASS\n   - Final-objective train/validation IC is mapped into `train_ic`/`validation_ic` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1394-1422`.\n   - Signed quality filter rejects single non-positive horizon and all non-positive blends at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1509-1541`; no `abs()` fallback observed.\n\n4. All invalid/non-positive horizons fallback T+5 baseline: PASS with reporting caveat\n   - Missing return columns produce excluded horizon metadata at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1222-1235`.\n   - All horizon failure triggers baseline `return_col` fallback at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1702-1735`; script sets `RETURN_HORIZON = 5` and `return_col = f'fwd_ret_{RETURN_HORIZON}'` at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:218-319`.\n   - Non-positive quality triggers baseline fallback at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1510-1541` and `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1715-1724`.\n\n5. PIT safety/no lookahead: gate and weights use train/validation only: PASS\n   - Per-horizon embargo before train/validation split at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1237-1268`.\n   - Gate validation uses `val_actual`, not test data, at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1286-1292`.\n   - Blend quality metrics are computed on `train_actual`/`val_actual` against final objective at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1394-1422`.\n\n6. JSON/reporting truthful for compliance: FAIL\n   - Same P1 finding: persisted fold metadata can describe an excluded horizon rather than the included/blended horizon.\n\n## Verification Run\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py -q`: 42 passed.\n- `python -m pytest tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py::TestP10GateTuningCLIPersist -q`: 3 passed.\n- Warnings observed: Vnstock update notice, pandas/numpy warnings, and pytest cache path warning. No test failures.\n- Code-review graph minimal-context call timed out after 120 seconds; direct source/test/report audit completed.\n\n## Final Verdict\n\n[NEEDS_FIX]","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":81,"totalLines":81,"truncated":false}},"title":".ly_state\\session\\audit_reports\\role20_p10_gate_tuning_compliance_audit_20260610.md","time":{"start":1781049098938,"end":1781049098951}},"id":"prt_eaecc8074001Ey3RQE9P0p8kyF","sessionID":"ses_15133c710fferRwlSke4x56SqF","messageID":"msg_eaecc62c5001xnvjTojxCduuVZ"}}
