m fix (select first included horizon) and optionally consider the better fix if it's not too complex.\n\nLooking at the code more carefully:\n- `horizon_results` contains `{horizon: (signal, quality_metrics)}` only for successful horizons\n- `horizon_details` contains diagnostics for ALL horizons (both included and excluded)\n\nUsing `horizon_results.keys()[0]` is the simplest and most correct fix.\n\n**ADD TEST:**\nI need to add a test that:\n1. Sets up a scenario where horizon 1 is excluded and horizon 3 is included\n2. Runs `run_fold()` (not just `_blend_horizon_signals()`)\n3. Checks that the resulting `FoldMetrics.gate_metadata` corresponds to horizon 3, not horizon 1\n\nTo make horizon 1 excluded, I can:\n- Make fwd_ret_1 missing in the data, OR\n- Make the gate fail for horizon 1, OR\n- Make the quality metrics non-positive for horizon 1\n\nLet me look at how existing tests set up data to understand the patterns.\n</thinking>\n\nNow I'll implement the fix and test. Let me create a task list for tracking:","time":{"start":1781049174073,"end":1781049189348}}}
